    </PointLabel>
    <Label Name="Title" Style="Heading" Text="The Upside-Down Candle" Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="16" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true" />
    <Label Name="Description" Style="Explanation" DecimalsToShow="1" Text="A lens bends the light from the flame so that the rays meet again on the other side, and there they draw a picture of the candle. Upside down! Hold a sheet of paper there and you would see it glowing.\n\nThree rays are easy to follow: the red one comes in level and leaves through the focus F′, the yellow one goes straight through the middle, and the blue one comes in through the focus F and leaves level.\n\nSlide the candle toward the lens: the picture grows and runs away. Inside F the rays never meet. Look back through the lens instead and you see a big candle the right way up: a magnifying glass.\n\nPull the handle on the lens to make it fatter. A fatter lens bends light more and its focus comes closer.\n\nCandle to lens: [u]. Lens to picture: [v]. Focus: [f]." Pin="TopRight" OffsetX="16" OffsetY="64" WrapWidth="400" Backdrop="true">
      <Dependency Name="u" />
      <Dependency Name="v" />
      <Dependency Name="f" />
    </Label>
  </Figures>
</Drawing>